-- ============================================================
-- Marksmanship: Go for the Throat
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Ranged critical hits cause your pet to generate 25/50 Focus, and
--  for ten seconds your pet's melee hits cause a bleed to be applied to the
--  target for 25/50% of the damage done that causes a high amount of threat.
--  (2 ranks) (Damage added like Deep Wounds / Unholy Blight)"
--
-- THE FOCUS HALF NEEDS NO CHANGE.  34952/34953 already store 24/49, which the
-- $s1 +1 rule renders as 25 and 50 -- exactly the agreed split.  Both payloads
-- are left untouched; only the talent descriptions are rewritten.  Resist the
-- urge to "fix" 24 to 50: that would display 51.
--
-- SHAPE: the crit is the HUNTER's, the bleed is the PET's, and a 10s window
-- joins them.  A ranged crit applies 200760 to the pet for 10s; while it is up,
-- EVERY pet melee hit rends.  That is two proc layers, and each is filtered in
-- exactly one place:
--
--   * "ranged critical hits"  -> core's spell_proc -34950 (HitMask 2), which
--     this pass does not touch.  It governs the whole talent aura, so both
--     Effect1 (Focus) and Effect2 (the frenzy) fire from the same crit.
--   * "melee hits"            -> spell_proc 200760, HitMask 0.  No crit
--     requirement here; requiring one in both places was the bug in the first
--     version of this talent.
--
-- Both proc-trigger effects live on one aura and both fire on the same proc, so
-- the trigger side needs no C++ at all -- the same property Against the Odds
-- relies on (see docs/hunter_implementation_notes.md).
--
-- Effect2 doubles as the rank store: its base points are 24/49, read back by
-- spell_hun_go_for_the_throat_bleed through OwnerTalentAmount(..., EFFECT_1).
-- A PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL effect still has an amount, so this costs nothing.
--
-- 200760 lands on the pet even though the triggered cast's explicit target is
-- the mob: AuraEffect::HandleProcTriggerSpellAuraProc casts
-- triggerCaster->CastSpell(triggerTarget, ...) (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:6914) with
-- the hunter as caster, and 200760's own EffectImplicitTargetA1 = 5
-- (TARGET_UNIT_PET) resolves m_caster->GetGuardianPet() for the effect.  This
-- is exactly how retail's Focus payload 34952 reaches the pet, which is why it
-- is safe to copy.
--
-- 200761 is handed a pre-computed amount by
-- Unit::CastDelayedSpellWithPeriodicAmount (Unit.cpp:16312), so every path that
-- would scale it again is switched off:
--
--   AttributesEx3 537198592 = SPELL_ATTR3_SUPPRESS_CASTER_PROCS  (0x00010000)
--                           | SPELL_ATTR3_ALWAYS_HIT             (0x00040000)
--                           | SPELL_ATTR3_IGNORE_CASTER_MODIFIERS(0x20000000)
--   AttributesEx2 536870916 = Deep Wounds' own 0x4
--                           | SPELL_ATTR2_CANT_CRIT              (0x20000000)
--
-- IGNORE_CASTER_MODIFIERS is the one that matters most: AuraEffect::
-- CalculateAmount runs SpellDamageBonusDone for PERIODIC_DAMAGE
-- (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:564), which is exactly how Beast Cleave's 200739
-- double-dipped before it carried this bit.
--
-- SPELL_ATTR3_SUPPRESS_TARGET_PROCS (0x00020000) is deliberately NOT set.  It
-- reads as "no initial aggro" and ThreatManager::AddThreat returns early on it
-- when the owner is not yet engaged (ThreatManager.cpp:399), which would kill
-- the threat half of this talent on exactly the pull it exists for.



